{"title":"Isosceles trapezoid","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><table style=\"border:thin solid black;padding:5px;float:right;margin:10px;\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"border:thin solid gray;\">\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/4/6c44731770aacefda73bf17a8a260f6120c94fa2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]draw((0,1)--(1,5)--(3,5)--(4,1)--cycle);[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\t\n</p>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><div class=\"magnify\" style=\"float: right;\">\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Enlarge.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/58/Enlarge.png/15px-Enlarge.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"15\" height=\"9\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/58/Enlarge.png/23px-Enlarge.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/58/Enlarge.png/30px-Enlarge.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure></div> An isosceles trapezoid\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>An <b>isosceles trapezoid</b> is a geometric figure that lies in a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Plane\" title=\"Plane\">plane</a>.  It is a specific type of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Trapezoid\" title=\"Trapezoid\">trapezoid</a> in which the legs have the same length. Its properties include:\n</p>\n<ul><li>congruent diagonals</li>\n<li>2 pairs of congruent <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle\" title=\"Angle\">angles</a></li>\n<li>one pair of congruent sides</li>\n<li>opposite angles are supplementary</li>\n<li>the segment joining the midpoints of the bases is perpendicular to the bases</li>\n<li>properties of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Trapezoid\" title=\"Trapezoid\">trapezoid</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Isosceles_trapezoid&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Trapezoid\" title=\"Trapezoid\">Trapezoid</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Isosceles_triangle\" title=\"Isosceles triangle\">Isosceles triangle</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Isosceles_trapezoid&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018091959\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.018 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.029 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 26/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 563/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 58/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 199/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.191      1 -total\n 48.54%    5.432      1 Template:Asy_image\n 48.41%    5.418      1 Template:Stub\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2202:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018091959 and revision id 242265. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}